{
 "about": "Per-country tables of the world answer key (kpc_world_key.py reads this file at start; a missing or malformed file stops the build: nothing is written). Moved out of the rule script on Nov 12 (KPC owner, 2026-11-12; D6), unchanged in content. Each table is keyed by country code, so an edit here moves only that country's area hash (kpc_area_hash.py slices this file per country). SRC = the country's built-in official layers, read in this order [label, reader, address, where-list or WFS type name]; layers from extra-layers.json and sheet-countries.json come after. EU = true: an EEA country (EU name rules: Natura codes in names, n2k kinds). GEN = the generic words dropped from names (regular expression), LOC = the same for EEA countries (the EU and English words are added in code). KINDS = [kind code, regular expression] read from a name. SIDE_NOT = words that are NOT a side (north / upper ...) in that country. TYPE_PREFER = POTA park type -> the layer labels preferred when several hold the pin. SPLIT_LAYERS = layers of extra-layers.json that are read WITHOUT the records a built-in source already reads (rest_where). notes = where each entry came from (not read by the builder, not in any hash).",
 "format": 1,
 "notes": {
  "AU": [
   "CAPAD 2024 terrestrial (DCCEEW, Australian Government).",
   "Next round C7 (Nov 5; owner's yes): Queensland state forests are read from the DESI layer 'Protected areas and forests of Queensland' (CC BY 4.0) with where esttype='SF'; the same layer as listed in extra-layers.json is read WITHOUT its SF (SPLIT_LAYERS.AU.rest_where), so no record comes twice.",
   "Oct 25: NSW Forestry Corporation, VIC DEECA (same data as DataVic PLM25, CC BY 4.0) and WA DBCA (CC BY-NC 4.0) state forest tenure. WA 'forest blocks' left out: management units, not the legal forest boundary."
  ],
  "DE": [
   "BfN Schutzgebiete WFS (Bundesamt fuer Naturschutz)."
  ],
  "GB": [
   "Natural England open data, NatureScot WFS, NRW Wales WFS. Northern Ireland (DAERA) left out: its terms forbid publishing maps without NIEA's written permission."
  ],
  "JP": [
   "Ministry of the Environment national parks via Esri Japan (nps_all, 34 national parks) + MLIT National Land Numerical Information A10 natural park areas (per prefecture; national file FY2010 A10-10 for the park-name codes; non-commercial licence, KPC is a non-commercial club)."
  ],
  "PL": [
   "Oct 25: the Slaskie voivodeship ORSIP copy of the GDOS register (nature and landscape complexes); no licence stated (regional copy of the national register)."
  ],
  "CH": [
   "Nov 7 world rebuild B6 (owner's yes): no EEA Natura 2000 source (Switzerland reports none; the empty source held CH every build). EEA nationally designated areas stay.",
   "Oct 18 (probe 2): the federal BAFU inventories (data.geo.admin.ch STAC, shapefiles in LV95); POTA's 151 CH 'Natural Monument' parks are BLN objects. Nov 8 (#76): the parks collection lost its _perimeter suffix.",
   "TYPE_PREFER.CH: the federal inventory of the park's POTA type decides when several records hold the pin."
  ],
  "NO": [
   "Nov 7 world rebuild B6 (owner's yes): no EEA Natura 2000 source (Norway reports none). EEA nationally designated areas stay."
  ],
  "FR": [
   "Oct 20: POTA's 'Biological Reserve' parks are ZNIEFF zones (MNHN / INPN): IGN Geoplateforme first, the Esri France copy only when the Geoplateforme answers nothing.",
   "2026-11-11 (KPC owner, world rules change approved): three more PatriNat layers (ZNIEFF type II sea, Conservatoire du littoral, RNN protection perimeters); Licence Ouverte as the research ledger records it."
  ],
  "CO": [
   "Oct 30 (owner's yes): RUNAP, the national register of protected areas (DNP)."
  ],
  "ZA": [
   "Oct 30 (owner's yes): DPME (from DFFE SAPAD) and SAPAD (DFFE)."
  ],
  "CL": [
   "Oct 30 (owner's yes): SIMBIO protected areas (MMA)."
  ],
  "*": [
   "EU countries (EU = true): the European Environment Agency layers (Natura 2000 sites + nationally designated areas, ex-CDDA), each filtered to the country; Oct 18 / Oct 19 (owner: 'go ahead')."
  ]
 },
